From 376ef1bd5c6e61d56e90c1ec9f3828e746f7fd44 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SableOS <noreply@sableos.invalid>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 18:24:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1102/1102] SableOS: Mobile Manager, App lock, Focus mode and
 Private Space pages

MOBILE_MANAGER_APP_CONTROLS_UX and PRIVATE_SPACE_DUAL_APPS_WORK_PROFILE_UX
as Settings-owned pages over Android's own mechanisms (model in the
previous patch):

* Mobile Manager (Settings > Apps > Mobile Manager, Settings > Sable,
  org.sableos.settings.MOBILE_MANAGER): one page with each control's
  state. Network access is the existing Network Manager (count of apps
  blocked on all networks; no second blocker or store). Background use
  opens Android's per-app battery list (hidden when the build turns it
  off). Notification/sync breakage warning and a plain list of what is
  not here yet (freezer, Student mode, autostart lists, site filters).
* App lock: launcher apps (never Settings, home, dialer, SMS app,
  keyboard, system UI) with switches; choices kept in Settings'
  device-protected storage. LineageOS 23.2 has no launch gate, so the
  page and every summary say "not enforced" and point to Private Space.
* Focus mode (org.sableos.settings.FOCUS_MODE): an AutomaticZenRule
  owned by Settings (priority apps, alarms, media, repeat callers only),
  so it is in Settings > Modes and Quick Settings too. "Apps that can
  notify you" switches Android's per-app channel bypass (the store the
  Modes app page writes; the page says it is shared with other modes).
  "Pause while Focus mode is on" suspends chosen apps with
  PackageManager.setPackagesSuspended (SUSPEND_APPS) and a "Paused by
  Focus mode" dialog whose button opens the page; only packages Settings
  suspended are released, on the rule's status broadcast and whenever
  the Focus or Mobile Manager page is shown. Schedules and the rest go
  to Android's own mode page.
* Private Space & Dual Apps: Private Space state (unavailable, not set
  up, locked, unlocked) opening Android's authentication/setup step;
  Dual Apps opening the cloned-apps list when the build enables it and
  allows an installed app (otherwise says why); work profile state and
  settings; App lock link and the profile-boundary note. Lock/unlock
  stays in Sable Start's All apps.

The Settings > Sable homepage row is now always shown (Mobile Manager
lives there). Mobile Manager and Private Space & Dual Apps are search
indexed; Mobile Manager is indexed once (from Apps). Every page gets the
Sable list keyboard (type-ahead, / search, Home/End, Page Up/Down).
